# Known-flaky behavior scenarios.
#
# Format: <scenario> <TAB> <reason>
# Lines starting with # are comments. When a listed scenario FAILS, the
# test-behavior recipe prints KNOWN-FLAKY + the reason and exits 0 (so
# batteries don't block on tracked issues). Re-run with strict=1 to treat
# a listed scenario's failure as a hard failure.
#
# Entries must carry a tracked issue reference and the observed failure
# signature — a flake without a reason is an unfiled bug, not a registry
# entry.

siege-settle	residual risk only (passes 3/3 pinned seeds after the expansion-cache fix): the ungrouped-unit recycle race still kills squads ~1 game-minute after formation (HIGH-priority mod bug, cec1b7a "Known remaining") — the retry machinery absorbs it, but seeds with pathological geography may exhaust the march budget. Keep listed until the recycle race is fixed. (logs: /tmp/rampant-behavior-siege-settle.out)
migration-settler	seed-sensitive (2 failures observed in ~6 random-seed runs, passes on re-run): the same formation-cadence dynamics as siege-settle (expansion quota epochs + the recycle race); the "settler leaves" assertion is position-based. Migrate to site-based assertion + scenario-lib, then re-evaluate. (logs: /tmp/rampant-behavior-migration-settler.out)
